    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nPerfectly positioned on this sought-after road, Number 14 Grosvenor Place is an impressive 4-6 bedroom, two-storey-over-basement Victorian residence of considerable charm and versatility. Retaining the generous proportions and architectural aesthetic of the Victorian era, this well-appointed, inviting home with a B energy-rating, is further enhanced by a perfectly oriented south-west facing mature rear garden with the added benefit of a large garage with direct access to Kenilworth Lane.\nBehind its attractive red-brick façade lies a versatile and generously proportioned, light-filled home extending over three levels with a total floor area of 196 sqm / 2110 sqft approx. The hall level comprises of a generous living room, south-west facing kitchen/dining room and guest WC. Upstairs are 4 bedrooms 3 of which are good doubles and a family bathroom complete with contemporary suite. Of particular note, is the basement accommodation. Currently separate to the main house, it comprises a kitchen, living/dining room, 2 bedrooms and shower room, providing the discerning buyer with many options for use from guest accommodation to a home office suite, or indeed an attractive home-and-income opportunity.\nThe location is superbly convenient. Grosvenor Place enjoys an enviable setting in the heart of Dublin 6, within a short stroll to Rathmines village and the vibrant amenities of Ranelagh. Residents benefit from an outstanding selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques, sporting facilities and renowned schools, while the nearby villages of Rathgar and Harold's Cross further enhance the area's appeal. The city centre is within easy reach by foot, bicycle or public transport, making this an ideal address for those seeking a lifestyle that combines suburban tranquillity with urban convenience.\nWarm in colour and character, superbly located and offering exceptional flexibility, No. 14 Grosvenor Place presents a great opportunity to acquire a very fine Victorian home in one of Dublin's most popular residential neighbourhoods. Viewing is recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall Level - \n\n\nPorch - \nOpen porch, tiled lobby.\n\nEntrance Hallway - \nWelcoming hallway with cornice, arch, dado rail, under stair storage with plumbing for washing machine, door to:\n\nGuest WC - \nWC, wash hand basin unit, extractor fan, tiled floor, wainscot walls.\n\nLiving Room - \nBay window with double glazed sash windows, handsome marble fireplace with open grate and cast-iron inset, cornicing and picture rail, high ceilings of 3.3m.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - \nLight-filled room with part free standing and fitted wall and floor units with double sink unit, extractor hood, induction hob, electric oven, tiled splashback, plumbed for dishwasher, tiled floor, high ceiling of 3.3m, coving, recessed lights, 2 large casement windows with window box seating, door to rear garden.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - \nCoving, light well, dado rail.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nDouble to front, built in wardrobes, double-glazed sash window, ceiling mounted radiator.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nBright double to rear, ceiling mounted radiator.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nCurrently in use as home office/music room. Casement window, attic access, ceiling mounted radiator.\n\nFamily bathroom - \nContemporary bathroom suite, fully tiled, bath with rain shower and handheld shower, inset shelving, WC, wash hand basin unit, backlit mirror, wall mounted cabinet, heated towel rail / radiator.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nAnother double to front, sash window, fitted shelving, ceiling mounted radiator.\n\nBasement - \nAccessed from front and rear gardens.\n\nSelf-contained apartment of 69 sqm approx - \n\n\nLobby - \nUnder stair storage, storage cupboards, through to:\n\nLiving / Dining Room - \nTiled fireplace with electric fire inset, shelving, coving, ceiling mounted electric radiator.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nSingle room to front, ceiling mounted electric radiator.\n\nKitchen - \nWall and floor units, stainless steel sink, wired for electric oven, plumbed for washing machine, part tiled splashback, free-standing butcher's block, ceiling mounted radiator, large storage closet.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nDouble room to rear, ceiling mounted radiator, large sash window overlooking rear patio and garden.\n\nShower Room - \nFully tiled, WC unit, step-in shower cubicle with electric shower, extractor fan, small window.\n\nGarden - \nOn-street permit parking to the front. Pedestrian access to the front, original wrought iron railings. Access to the apartment and main house. The mature rear garden enjoys a wonderful south-westerly aspect. Laid in lawn, it is bordered by cut-stone walls with mature shrubs, trees and flowering plants. Access from here to the block-built shed with WC. Door to the large garage, which measures L5.24m x W3.57m. There is rear access to Kenilworth Lane.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Handsome Victorian terraced home with BER B</li><li>South-westerly rear garden</li><li>Large garage to rear with access to Kenilworth Lane</li><li>Versatile accommodation of 196 sqm / 2110 sqft approx (127 sqm in main house plus 69 sqm in basement apt)</li><li>Solar panels (which heat the water)</li><li>Energy efficient Infrared radiators in the basement and top floor</li><li>Oil heating on the hall level floor</li><li>Double glazed sash windows at the front and double glazed casement windows at the back</li><li>Superb location within walking distance of Rathmines, Rathgar, Ranelagh and the city centre</ul>"
      },
